.SH NAME
osdistro \- a logical object definition in the xCAT database.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBosdistro Attributes:\fR  \fIarch\fR, \fIbasename\fR, \fIdirpaths\fR, \fImajorversion\fR, \fIminorversion\fR, \fIosdistroname\fR, \fItype\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Logical objects of this type are stored in the xCAT database in one or more tables.  Use the following commands
to manipulate the objects: \fBmkdef\fR, \fBchdef\fR, \fBlsdef\fR, and \fBrmdef\fR.  These commands will take care of
knowing which tables the object attributes should be stored in.  The attribute list below shows, in
parentheses, what tables each attribute is stored in.
.SH "osdistro Attributes:"
.IX Header "osdistro Attributes:"
.IP "\fBarch\fR (osdistro.arch)" 6
.IX Item "arch (osdistro.arch)"
The OS distro arch (e.g. x86_64)
.IP "\fBbasename\fR (osdistro.basename)" 6
.IX Item "basename (osdistro.basename)"
The OS base name (e.g. rhels)
.IP "\fBdirpaths\fR (osdistro.dirpaths)" 6
.IX Item "dirpaths (osdistro.dirpaths)"
Directory paths where OS distro is store. There could be multiple paths if OS distro has more than one ISO image. (e.g. /install/rhels6.2/x86_64,...)
.IP "\fBmajorversion\fR (osdistro.majorversion)" 6
.IX Item "majorversion (osdistro.majorversion)"
The OS distro major version.(e.g. 6)
.IP "\fBminorversion\fR (osdistro.minorversion)" 6
.IX Item "minorversion (osdistro.minorversion)"
The OS distro minor version. (e.g. 2)
.IP "\fBosdistroname\fR (osdistro.osdistroname)" 6
.IX Item "osdistroname (osdistro.osdistroname)"
Unique name (e.g. rhels6.2\-x86_64)
.IP "\fBtype\fR (osdistro.type)" 6
.IX Item "type (osdistro.type)"
Linux or AIX
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBmkdef\|(1)\fR, \fBchdef\|(1)\fR, \fBlsdef\|(1)\fR, \fBrmdef\|(1)\fR
